# Local Manifests for LGE SDM845 Custom Android Builds

Personal local manifests for Android ROM builds. Managed dynamically via separate branches to support multiple device families and SoC platforms.

---

## How to Use
To fetch the required repositories for your target build, follow the instructions below.

### Prerequisites
Make sure you have already initialized your ROM's source tree using `repo init` (e.g., LineageOS, EvolutionX, PixelOS, etc.) and that you are currently in the root directory of your android source code.

---

### Step 1: Create the target directory (if it doesn't exist)
Run this command in the root of your source tree:
```bash
   mkdir -p .repo/local_manifests
```

### Step 2: Download the XML directly from the specific branch
Example for the LG SDM845 (G7 / V35 / V40) platform on EvolutionX 12:
```bash
    curl -L -o .repo/local_manifests/LGE_SDM845_Family.xml https://raw.githubusercontent.com/DanCS1995/local_manifests/lge_sdm845_seventeen-cnb-evox/LGE_SDM845_Family.xml
```

### Step 3: Download the Lineage SDM845 Hals Manifest
This file re-tracks all the SDM845 Hals that were droped temporarily:
```bash
    curl -L -o .repo/local_manifests/LGE_SDM845_Lineage_Hals.xml https://raw.githubusercontent.com/DanCS1995/local_manifests/lge_sdm845_seventeen-cnb-evox/LGE_SDM845_Lineage_Hals.xml
```

### Step 4: Add "os_pickup_qssi.bp for SDM845" line into manifest
Open the ".repo/manifest/snippets/lineage.xml" file. Locate the  line(92) "linkfile src="os_pickup_qssi.bp" dest="hardware/qcom-caf/sm8750/Android.bp", and add this line bellow and save the file:
```bash
 <linkfile src="os_pickup_qssi.bp" dest="hardware/qcom-caf/sdm845/Android.bp" />
```

### Step 5: Synchronize Source Trees
Once the local manifest is in place, trigger repo sync to clean up conflicting default projects and fetch the custom repositories:
```bash
    repo sync -c -j$(nproc --all) --force-sync --no-clone-bundle --no-tags
```


